The "Group by" selector writes a flat `groupBy` property and (for kanban) updates `kanban.groupByField`, but the runtime view schema builders read `options.kanban.groupField` (and warn on flat keys in dev). This means changing Group by in the panel may not actually change kanban grouping and can trigger spec-compliance warnings. Consider removing the flat `groupBy` write and updating `kanban.groupField` (optionally mirroring to `kanban.groupByField` for backward compatibility) instead.
```suggestion
                                    const value = e.target.value;
                                    if (viewType === 'kanban') {
                                        // For kanban, use options.kanban.groupField as the canonical key
                                        handleTypeOptionChange('kanban', 'groupField', value);
                                        // Mirror to groupByField for backward compatibility
                                        handleTypeOptionChange('kanban', 'groupByField', value);
                                    } else {
                                        // Preserve existing flat groupBy behavior for non-kanban views
                                        updateDraft('groupBy', value);
```

For kanban, the panel renders both the universal "Group by" row and a type-specific "Group by field" select. These controls can diverge (type-specific updates only `kanban.groupByField`), and it’s redundant UX. Suggest keeping a single source of truth (either remove the type-specific row for kanban or have both update the same underlying key(s), e.g. `kanban.groupField`).
```suggestion
                                            value={draft.kanban?.groupField || draft.kanban?.groupByField || ''}
                                            onChange={(e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLSelectElement>) => {
                                                const value = e.target.value;
                                                handleTypeOptionChange('kanban', 'groupField', value);
                                                handleTypeOptionChange('kanban', 'groupByField', value);
                                            }}
```

The export toggle’s checked state is derived from `hasExport`, which is true when `draft.exportOptions` is defined. If `exportOptions` is set, toggling "Allow export" off only updates `allowExport` but the switch will remain on (and export remains enabled) because `exportOptions` is still present. Consider making the switch state depend on `allowExport` (and/or clearing `exportOptions` when disabling) so the control can actually turn export off.
```suggestion
                                checked={draft.allowExport !== false && hasExport}
                                onCheckedChange={(checked: boolean) => {
                                    updateDraft('allowExport', checked);
                                    if (!checked) {
                                        updateDraft('exportOptions', undefined);
                                    }
                                }}
```

The row height control uses `role="radiogroup"`/`role="radio"` but doesn’t implement the expected roving tabIndex/arrow-key keyboard interaction, and each radio’s `aria-label` is the raw internal value ("short", "medium", etc.) rather than a localized label. Consider using native radio inputs or adding keyboard handling + localized labels to match ARIA radio patterns.
```suggestion
                            <div
                                className="flex gap-0.5"
                                data-testid="appearance-rowHeight"
                                aria-label={t('console.objectView.rowHeight')}
                            >
                                {ROW_HEIGHT_OPTIONS.map(opt => {
                                    const isSelected = (draft.rowHeight || 'short') === opt.value;
                                    const label = t(`console.objectView.rowHeight.${opt.value}`);
                                    return (
                                        <label
                                            key={opt.value}
                                            className={`h-7 w-7 rounded border flex items-center justify-center cursor-pointer ${
                                                isSelected
                                                    ? 'border-primary bg-primary/10 text-primary'
                                                    : 'border-input text-muted-foreground hover:bg-accent/50'
                                            }`}
                                            title={label}
                                        >
                                            <input
                                                type="radio"
                                                name="rowHeight"
                                                value={opt.value}
                                                checked={isSelected}
                                                onChange={() => updateDraft('rowHeight', opt.value)}
                                                aria-label={label}
                                                className="sr-only"
                                            />
                                            <div
                                                className={`flex flex-col items-center justify-center w-4 h-4 ${opt.gapClass}`}
                                                data-testid={`row-height-${opt.value}`}
                                            >
                                                <div className="w-3.5 h-px bg-current rounded-full" />
                                                <div className="w-3.5 h-px bg-current rounded-full" />
                                                <div className="w-3.5 h-px bg-current rounded-full" />
                                            </div>
                                        </label>
                                    );
                                })}
```
